## Lower Bound: 12 racks are necessary

**Construction.** Consider 58 clusters of size 34 and 1 cluster of size 18. Total = 58 × 34 + 18 = 1972 + 18 = 1990. Each cluster size ≤ 39. ✓

**11 racks are insufficient.** In any rack of capacity 199, at most ⌊199/34⌋ = 5 clusters of size 34 fit, since 6 × 34 = 204 > 199. Across 11 racks, at most 11 × 5 = 55 clusters of size 34 can be accommodated. But we have 58 such clusters. No rearrangement helps—the constraint 6×34 > 199 is absolute. Therefore 11 racks cannot hold this configuration, so **at least 12 racks** are required. ∎

---

## Upper Bound: 12 racks always suffice

**Algorithm.** Sort clusters in decreasing order of size. Apply First-Fit Decreasing (FFD): place each cluster into the first rack that has enough remaining capacity.

**Claim:** FFD uses at most 12 racks.

**Proof by contradiction.** Suppose FFD uses 13 or more racks. Let *s* be the size of the first cluster placed in rack 13. Since clusters are processed in decreasing order, every cluster in racks 1–12 has size ≥ *s*.

When cluster *s* was placed in rack 13, it did not fit in any of racks 1–12. Therefore each rack 1–12 has load ≥ 200 − *s* (since load + *s* > 199 and all values are integers).

**Case 1: *s* ≤ 34.** Then each rack 1–12 has load ≥ 200 − 34 = 166. Total load in racks 1–12 ≥ 12 × 166 = 1992 > 1990. This exceeds the total size of all clusters—contradiction.

**Case 2: *s* ≥ 35.** Each rack 1–12 has load ≥ 200 − *s* ≥ 200 − 39 = 161. Since every item in these racks has size ≤ 39, each rack must contain at least ⌈(200 − *s*)/39⌉ clusters. For *s* ∈ [35, 39]:
- (200 − *s*) ranges from 161 to 165, and ⌈(200−*s*)/39⌉ = 5 (since 4 × 39 = 156 < 161 ≤ 200−*s*).

So racks 1–12 contain at least 12 × 5 = 60 clusters, each of size ≥ *s* ≥ 35. Their total size ≥ 60 × 35 = 2100 > 1990—contradiction.

Both cases yield contradictions, so FFD uses **at most 12 racks**. ∎

---

## Conclusion

The lower bound (12, from the explicit construction of 58 clusters of size 34 + 1 cluster of size 18) matches the upper bound (12, from the FFD guarantee). Therefore:

**The minimum number of cooling racks required is 12.**

